msgctxt "#30011"
msgid "yt-dlp could not resolve this video"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30012"
msgid "No playable stream found"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30013"
msgid "Open settings"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30100"
msgid "Playback"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30101"
msgid "Fall back to a progressive stream"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30102"
msgid "If no HLS manifest is offered, play the best single file that carries both video and audio. Most YouTube videos no longer have one, so this rarely helps."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30103"
msgid "Send the legacy manifest_type property"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30104"
msgid "InputStream Adaptive 21 detects HLS from the mime type. Enable this only if playback fails with a manifest type error on an older build."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30110"
msgid "Picture & sound (YouTube)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30111"
msgid "Maximum resolution"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30112"
msgid "Variants above this height are removed from the manifest before InputStream Adaptive sees it. \"No limit\" leaves the choice to its adaptive logic."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30113"
msgid "No limit"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30114"
msgid "2160p (4K)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30115"
msgid "1440p"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30116"
msgid "1080p"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30117"
msgid "720p"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30118"
msgid "480p"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30119"
msgid "Video codec"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30120"
msgid "YouTube offers H.264 and VP9 up to 1080p and VP9 alone above it. \"H.264 only\" caps playback at 1080p; \"VP9 only\" needs hardware VP9 decoding. A choice that would leave nothing to play is ignored."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30121"
msgid "Auto"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30122"
msgid "H.264 only"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30123"
msgid "VP9 only"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30124"
msgid "Audio track"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30125"
msgid "InputStream Adaptive on Kodi 21 starts YouTube's packed-ADTS audio silent until the first seek. \"fMP4 (fixed)\" replaces it with YouTube's DASH AAC track in fMP4, read by the same demuxer as the video, so sound plays from the first frame. \"As published\" keeps YouTube's own audio (silent-until-seek) for diagnosis."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30126"
msgid "fMP4 (fixed)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30127"
msgid "As published"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30140"
msgid "Subtitles"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30141"
msgid "Download subtitles"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30142"
msgid "Downloads every subtitle track the video's author uploaded, as files Kodi labels by language. Kodi then picks the one matching its own \"Preferred subtitle language\" setting. YouTube's automatic captions are not used: they are machine output, and the translated ones require browser TLS impersonation that no Kodi add-on can provide."
msgstr ""






msgctxt "#30150"
msgid "Rewrite YouTube's manifest (enables the settings below)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30151"
msgid "YouTube only: videos from other sites always play with their manifest as published, whatever is set here — the rewrite fixes YouTube's own quirks, which other sites do not have. The settings below work by rewriting YouTube's HLS master playlist and serving the copy from 127.0.0.1 to InputStream Adaptive. Switch this off to hand over YouTube's manifest untouched, exactly as version 1.0 did — no rewriting, no local server."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30152"
msgid "Quality selection"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30153"
msgid "\"Adaptive\" keeps every allowed variant and lets InputStream Adaptive switch by measured bandwidth. \"Best available\" keeps only the tallest, highest-bitrate variant that passed the codec and resolution settings, so it plays at that quality from the first second — and buffers rather than adapts if the connection cannot carry it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30154"
msgid "Adaptive"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30155"
msgid "Best available"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30156"
msgid "Local manifest server port"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30157"
msgid "Rewritten manifests are served to InputStream Adaptive from 127.0.0.1 on this port. Change it only if another add-on already uses it (plugin.video.youtube uses 50152); the server restarts on its own."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30160"
msgid "yt-dlp"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30161"
msgid "Update channel"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30162"
msgid "Where new yt-dlp versions come from. Nightly is built every day from the project's main branch, and fixes for YouTube changes arrive there first. Stable is released less often (yt-dlp promises a release at least every 90 days). After switching, use \"Check for updates now\"."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30163"
msgid "Nightly"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30164"
msgid "Stable"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30165"
msgid "Update automatically"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30166"
msgid "Checks for a new yt-dlp a minute after Kodi starts and then once a day, in the background. A new version is used only after it has been checked against Kodi's Python: one that needs a newer Python is rejected and the current one stays."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30167"
msgid "Check for updates now"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30168"
msgid "Checks the selected channel right away and shows the result."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30170"
msgid "yt-dlp {} is up to date"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30171"
msgid "yt-dlp updated to {}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30172"
msgid "yt-dlp update not applied: {}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30173"
msgid "yt-dlp update failed: {}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30174"
msgid "Checking for yt-dlp updates…"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30180"
msgid "Cast"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30181"
msgid "Receive casts from the YouTube app"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30182"
msgid "Kodi appears as a TV in the YouTube app on your phone: tap the cast button and pick it. Videos then play here through yt-dlp, and the phone works as the remote. While this is on, Kodi keeps one connection to youtube.com open so the phone can reach it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30183"
msgid "Name shown on the phone"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30184"
msgid "Leave empty for Kodi's own name followed by \"(yt-dlp)\", e.g. \"CoreELEC (yt-dlp)\" — different from what TubeCast shows, should both be installed."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30185"
msgid "Discoverable on the local network"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30186"
msgid "Answers the YouTube app's search on the local network (SSDP and DIAL), so Kodi shows up in the cast menu by itself. Switch off to connect only with a TV code."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30187"
msgid "Link with a TV code"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30188"
msgid "Shows a code to type into the YouTube app (Settings → Watch on TV → Enter TV code). Works when the phone is on another network, or when the local search does not find Kodi. A linked phone stays linked across restarts."
msgstr ""


msgctxt "#30191"
msgid "{} connected"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30192"
msgid "{} disconnected"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30193"
msgid "Casting is switched off in the settings"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30194"
msgid "Not connected to YouTube yet — try again in a moment"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30195"
msgid "Could not get a TV code: {}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30196"
msgid "In the YouTube app on the phone open Settings → Watch on TV → Enter TV code, and type:"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30197"
msgid "Phone linked"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30198"
msgid "TubeCast is enabled as well, so the phone lists two receivers for this box. Disable one of them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30169"
msgid "the downloaded one does not work"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30175"
msgid "Version in use"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30176"
msgid "Last check"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30177"
msgid "downloaded"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30178"
msgid "bundled copy"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30179"
msgid "not checked yet"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30200"
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30201"
msgid "Enable all diagnostics"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30202"
msgid "Turns on every switch below at once — for a complete log to report a problem with. Each switch writes to kodi.log at INFO level, so Kodi's own debug logging is not needed. Without any switch the add-on logs only warnings, errors and one summary line per playback, update check and phone connection."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30204"
msgid "Resolving the video"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30205"
msgid "yt-dlp's progress while it resolves a video, how long it took, and what YouTube offered: whether there is an HLS manifest, resolutions and codecs, audio tracks, subtitles. Shows at which step resolving fails and why a quality is missing."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30206"
msgid "yt-dlp verbose mode"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30207"
msgid "yt-dlp's own verbose output: its version, Python, OpenSSL and certifi, JavaScript runtimes, the YouTube clients it tries. Long — for problems inside yt-dlp itself."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30208"
msgid "Manifest rewriting"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30209"
msgid "The variants and audio groups before and after each filter (resolution, codec, quality), the fMP4 audio that replaces YouTube's, and where the rewritten manifest is served. Keeps a copy of the original manifest next to the rewritten one in Kodi's temp folder."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30210"
msgid "Manifest server requests"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30211"
msgid "Every request InputStream Adaptive makes to the add-on's local manifest server, with its status and size — whether the rewritten playlists were actually fetched."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30212"
msgid "Subtitle downloads"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30213"
msgid "Which subtitle tracks the author uploaded, which are downloaded, and each file's size and download time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30214"
msgid "Kodi player: decoder, quality, buffering"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30215"
msgid "Watches Kodi's player while it plays what the add-on resolved: the video and audio decoder and whether decoding runs in hardware, quality changes made by InputStream Adaptive, every stall to buffer with its length, and a summary at the end."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30216"
msgid "Network and updates"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30217"
msgid "HTTP requests of the add-on"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30218"
msgid "Every request the add-on itself makes — manifest, audio index, subtitles, yt-dlp updates, the cast session — with status, size and time, and once the certificates it verifies against. Query strings and signatures are left out. yt-dlp's own requests are in its verbose mode."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30219"
msgid "yt-dlp updater"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30220"
msgid "Each step of a yt-dlp update check: the published checksum, the download, the validation against Kodi's Python and the clean-up of older copies."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30221"
msgid "Cast events"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30222"
msgid "Every step of casting: discovery answers, pairing, the YouTube session, each command from the phone (<-) and each answer to it (->)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30223"
msgid "Cast: raw protocol traffic"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30224"
msgid "The cast protocol as received and sent, including the frequent position reports and keep-alives. Very long; for when YouTube changes something in the protocol."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30225"
msgid "Local network discovery: every packet"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30226"
msgid "Every SSDP packet that reaches Kodi, not only the YouTube app's searches, and the headers of each DIAL request. For \"the phone does not see Kodi\": it shows whether the phone's searches arrive at all."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30227"
msgid "Service"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30228"
msgid "Background service"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30229"
msgid "The add-on's service: start-up and shutdown with their timing, the manifest server, settings changes as they are applied, and the update schedule."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30230"
msgid "Web interface"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30231"
msgid "Enable the web interface"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30232"
msgid "A page for any browser on the local network: paste a link to a video or a playlist — YouTube or any other site yt-dlp supports — to play it or add it to the queue, see what is playing, seek, pause, stop, and read the add-on's log. Off by default, because it opens a port on the network."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30233"
msgid "Address"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30234"
msgid "Open this address in a browser on a phone or computer in the same network. A link added to it as ?play=<link> is played right away."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30235"
msgid "Require a PIN"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30236"
msgid "Off: anyone on the local network can use the page. On: a browser asks once for this PIN and remembers it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30237"
msgid "PIN"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30238"
msgid "New PIN"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30239"
msgid "Replaces the PIN; every browser that knew the old one has to enter the new one."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30240"
msgid "Port"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30241"
msgid "The page is served on this port, on every address of the box. Change it only if another program already uses it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30242"
msgid "Web interface requests"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30243"
msgid "Every request to the web interface: address of the browser, method, path, status."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30244"
msgid "New web interface PIN: {}"
msgstr ""
